tz, who won Donald Trump's endorsement in July and has raised roughly $2.4 million, matching Mrvan's haul while holding more cash on hand. National Republicans have signaled they will put resources into flipping the district.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the picture rests on expert ratings, fundraising, and prediction markets. Rating outlets split between Likely Democratic and Safe Democratic, and markets price a Democratic win around 96 percent. Recent coverage shows Mrvan campaigning on labor legislation and disaster response, while Regnitz has pledged loyalty to Trump. The challenger's resources make this a genuine contest, but the weight of the evidence keeps it in Likely Democratic territory.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9569, "margin": 11.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9243, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9241, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9308, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9246, "margin": 10.6}]}